interpretation:
Slice A creates local packet/corridor model contracts only.

It proves:
- only Root can create an ActionCommitPacket;
- human approval is scoped evidence only;
- LLM, DRS, AVF, and GT/LGT actors cannot create an ActionCommitPacket;
- the packet is Supplier A mock-payment scoped only;
- Supplier B, shipment release, real bank, real supplier API, real warehouse API, and real-world effects are forbidden;
- the packet adapter binding must be included in packet scope allowed adapters;
- corridor child steps must bind to the same packet_id as their parent packet;
- corridor child steps cannot widen allowed scope, action surface, TTL, adapter, amount, creditor, payment slot, or idempotency;
- receipt is evidence only;
- receipt cannot create future permission, action permission, FinalOutput, shipment release, Supplier B authorization, production DRS record, or effects;
- receipt validation inherits source packet validity;
- reasoning does not restart after Root.

